    "payload": {
      "rootMessageId": "request-ff700c26-0a97-4055-9929-1d34a00465e8",
      "requestId": "request-ff700c26-0a97-4055-9929-1d34a00465e8",
      "runId": "run-1984752c-02c7-40f9-beef-348f740afc5e",
      "requestContextId": "context-07e6556a-2350-41af-a71f-f6957e9d60f1",
      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "content": "Detection complete. All three approximants independently converge on the same binary black hole signal.\n\n## Results\n\n| approximant | peak SNR | total mass (M☉) | best (m1, m2) | peak time |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SEOBNRv4_opt | 17.9110 | 44 | (20, 24) | 105.00 s |\n| IMRPhenomD | 18.0696 | 44 | (23, 21) | 105.00 s |\n| TaylorT4 | 17.2744 | 44 | (22, 22) | 104.98 s |\n\nResults written to `workspace/detection_results.csv`:\n```csv\napproximant,snr,total_mass\nSEOBNRv4_opt,17.9110,44\nIMRPhenomD,18.0696,44\nTaylorT4,17.2744,44\n```\n\n## What was done\n- **Data**: `H1:TEST-STRAIN` from `PyCBC_T2_2.gwf` — 128 s at 4096 Hz.\n- **Conditioning**: high-pass at 15 Hz → resample to 2048 Hz → crop 2 s each end (124 s) → Welch PSD (4 s segments) with `inverse_spectrum_truncation`.\n- **Matched filtering**: time-domain templates (`f_lower=20 Hz`), since SEOBNRv4_opt and TaylorT4 aren't available in frequency domain in this PyCBC build. Full grid of mass1, mass2 = 10–40 (integer steps) = 2883 templates, 0 failures.\n\nThe signal is unambiguous: all three waveform models locate the merger at t≈105 s with peak SNR ≈ 17–18, and all agree on a **total mass of 44 M☉** (near-equal-mass binary, ~22+22). The strongest single template is IMRPhenomD at SNR 18.07.",
      "text": "Detection complete. All three approximants independently converge on the same binary black hole signal.\n\n## Results\n\n| approximant | peak SNR | total mass (M☉) | best (m1, m2) | peak time |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SEOBNRv4_opt | 17.9110 | 44 | (20, 24) | 105.00 s |\n| IMRPhenomD | 18.0696 | 44 | (23, 21) | 105.00 s |\n| TaylorT4 | 17.2744 | 44 | (22, 22) | 104.98 s |\n\nResults written to `workspace/detection_results.csv`:\n```csv\napproximant,snr,total_mass\nSEOBNRv4_opt,17.9110,44\nIMRPhenomD,18.0696,44\nTaylorT4,17.2744,44\n```\n\n## What was done\n- **Data**: `H1:TEST-STRAIN` from `PyCBC_T2_2.gwf` — 128 s at 4096 Hz.\n- **Conditioning**: high-pass at 15 Hz → resample to 2048 Hz → crop 2 s each end (124 s) → Welch PSD (4 s segments) with `inverse_spectrum_truncation`.\n- **Matched filtering**: time-domain templates (`f_lower=20 Hz`), since SEOBNRv4_opt and TaylorT4 aren't available in frequency domain in this PyCBC build. Full grid of mass1, mass2 = 10–40 (integer steps) = 2883 templates, 0 failures.\n\nThe signal is unambiguous: all three waveform models locate the merger at t≈105 s with peak SNR ≈ 17–18, and all agree on a **total mass of 44 M☉** (near-equal-mass binary, ~22+22). The strongest single template is IMRPhenomD at SNR 18.07.",
